110 < 1 ## Jev's gate reading, live
111 < 1 
112 < 1 `gate_jev_replay_probe.mjs` replays every labelled gate disagreement in the operator's untracked
113 < 1 `docs/superpowers/plans/` through the real Jev (key in `~/.ultrapowers/typesafe.env`): each round where
114 < 1 the agent reader and Jev differ and `right` is set, its diet rebuilt by `extract_gate_input.py` (with the
115 < 1 tally's `base` when that round saw one) and skipped when the task no longer hashes the same, then read
116 < 1 by `gate_jev.ts` (never `--record`). Beside them, two known-bad controls (`uncaught-output`,
117 < 1 `pinned-by-sibling`) must each still read `fail` in a majority. It spends `reps` × (rounds + 2) calls.
118 < 1 It counts the wrong fails (agent right, Jev failed) that now pass, the right fails (Jev right) that
119 < 1 still fail, and the agreed fails (agent and Jev both failed it, #1528) that now pass; the summary reports
120 < 1 `agreed fails now pass N of M`, so an `of 0` shows the check is vacuous. Exit 0 when the controls hold, no
121 < 1 agreed fail now passes and at least two thirds of the wrong fails now pass; any agreed fail that now
122 < 1 passes exits 1. The scoring lives in `_gate_replay_helpers.mjs`, run by `test_gate_jev_replay.mjs` in the suite.
123 < 1 
124 < 1 Run it before any change to the `authoring_gate` questions, to `gate_reading`, or to
125 < 1 `extract_gate_input.py`'s `base`:
126 < 1 
127 < 1     node fleet/tests/gate_jev_replay_probe.mjs docs/superpowers/plans 3
128 < 1 
129 < 1 When a change moves two things at once, flipping one `gate_reading` cell back measures the other
130 < 1 change alone.
131 < 1 
132 < 1 Readings of the earlier caught_v2 wording (before #1528 narrowed it to wiring), 2026-10-01, `jev-1.13.0`, n=15 wrong fails from 10 plans dated 2026-09-29..30, 3 reads each,
133 < 1 majority:
134 < 1 
135 < 1 | Reading | Wrong fails still failing |
136 < 1 |---|---|
137 < 1 | caught/read (before) | 14 of 15 |
138 < 1 | caught/dropped | 6 of 15 |
139 < 1 | caught_v2/read | 9 of 15 |
140 < 1 | caught_v2/dropped | 2 of 15 |
141 < 1 
142 < 1 Both controls failed 3 of 3 under every reading. The one round Jev was right on, rebuilt by hand (its
143 < 1 round-1 diet is not replayable), failed 1 of 3 before and 0 of 3 after: the change gives up that catch.
144 < 1 
145 < 1 Readings of the narrowed caught_v2 (#1528) with `own_files: dropped`, 2026-10-02 06:40 UTC, `jev-1.13.0`,
146 < 1 n=23 wrong fails from the plans dated 2026-09-29..10-01, 1 read each (`gate_jev_replay_probe.mjs` with no
147 < 1 `reps`), exit 0:
148 < 1 
149 < 1 | Reading | Wrong fails still failing | Agreed fails now passing |
150 < 1 |---|---|---|
151 < 1 | caught_v2 (narrowed)/dropped | 3 of 23 (all 2026-09-29-fast-boot: task 1 r2, task 3 r5, task 4 r1) | 0 of 0 |
152 < 1 
153 < 1 Both controls read `fail`. No labelled agreed-fail round was replayable, so the two-sided check is
154 < 1 vacuous on this window; it gains a count only once runs record rounds where both readers failed.
